4. Modifications and Improvements

You are permitted to modify, improve, and extend Say It.

When contributing improvements to the official GitHub repository:

1. Create a separate branch for your work, or submit your changes through a fork.
2. Submit your proposed improvements through a pull request targeting the appropriate branch.
3. Do not directly push changes to the official "main" branch.
4. Keep proposed changes isolated from the official "main" branch until they are reviewed and accepted by the project maintainer.

The "main" branch is reserved for changes accepted and integrated by the project maintainer.

You may maintain your own fork or separate branch containing modifications, provided you follow this license when using or distributing the Project.

Submitting a contribution does not guarantee that it will be accepted or merged.

